        "txtField": {
          "txtElements": [
            {
              "title": "Keypoints",
              "type": "list",
              "elements": [
                "Master @faculty of applied computer science",
                "Thesis: Leveraging Agent Based Models for the generation of inertial measurement unit data"
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "Study Projects",
              "type": "list",
              "elements": ["SpotOn", "Rasa ChatBot", "Smart Grocery List"],
              "options": {
                "elementLinks": {"SpotOn": "https://gitlab.com/studies4644235/spoton/-/tree/8a6f6e45d254e7f1d0d3208de9ce7fbc02117135/", "Rasa ChatBot":  "https://gitlab.com/studies4644235/smartgrocerylist/-/tree/097768d7a997ede817fb5b9f1c7cf18f31aceaa3/", "Smart Grocery List": "https://gitlab.com/studies4644235/rasachatbot/-/tree/0a8bc3d2e73b11d5413de6321c293fa5be724c20/"}
              }
            },
            {
              "title": "Summary",
              "type": "text",
              "elements": [
                "The program is specifically designed for domain experts to learn and apply data science and algorithmic approaches to problems in the humanities and social sciences. I learned the skills necessary to cover the intersection of privacy and mobility from a software-technical perspective. The goal of my thesis was to understand hurdles, feasibility, and chances of utilizing stochastic traffic models for sensor data generation, an approach underrepresented in current research. For my thesis, I developed a non deep-learning method for data generation and compared it to state-of-the-art deep-learning approaches."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "detail": {
            "date": "04/2022 - 01/2025",
            "link": "",
            "organization": "Otto-Friedrich University | sepp med GmbH"
          },
          "subtitle": "Adding software technical expertise to the mix"
        }
      },
